  - adversarial robustness
  - workforce augmentation
abstract: >-
  The Pro-Worker AI Benchmark (PWB) measures whether large language
  models augment human cognition or substitute for it. The benchmark
  operationalizes the human-AI complementarity literature into eleven
  behavioral dimensions (cognitive forcing, contrastive explanation,
  skill preservation, draft annotation, uncertainty transparency,
  complementarity, adversarial resilience, anti-sycophancy,
  metacognitive calibration, appropriate reliance, ethical surfacing).
  It spans 320 evaluation instances across three layers: 200
  single-turn behavioral probes, 16 multi-turn scenarios (5 turns
  each), and 40 adversarial stress tests. Responses are scored by a
  three-judge LLM panel from distinct families with median
  aggregation, across five runs per prompt. Across seven open-weight
  models from six families (GLM 5.1, Gemma 4 31B, DeepSeek V3.2,
  GPT-oss 120B, Nemotron-Cascade 30B, Qwen3.5 27B, Devstral-2 123B),
  baseline Pro-Worker Index ranges from 25.4 to 39.2; a pro-worker
  system prompt raises it to 56.9 to 82.3 (Cohen's d up to 1.30,
  p less than 10^-39). The effect persists at multi-turn (d = 1.61)
  and adversarial (d = 1.41) layers. All prompts, rubrics, scoring
  code, and per-run results are released.
